  "_read_me": "Sound design lives here. `at` accepts: \"scenes\" (one cue on every scene start), \"<section id>\" (its start), \"<section id>+0.85\" (offset into that section), or an absolute second. Section-relative cues survive a re-record; absolute seconds do not. Keep <= 1 cue per second and never land a cue on a word's first syllable. The bed is instrumental, loop-safe, and set so it measures ~13 LU below the -16 LUFS VO (0.15 on a -12.5 LUFS track = -29 LUFS); no ducking — the gap is the duck.",
